#: templates/admin/help.php:11
msgid "Settings safety"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/help.php:12
msgid "Activation and the first request after upgrading reset historical theme-capability grants on built-in WordPress content roles. Missing Administrator theme-management grants are restored only when legacy settings selected Administrator. Changed roles are backed up first. Deactivation ends temporary grants and restrictions. Ordinary uninstall preserves configuration."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/help.php:13
msgid "Cleanup covers edit_theme_options, edit_themes, update_themes, delete_themes, install_themes and upload_themes. Explicit denials and unrelated permissions are preserved. Custom roles have no WordPress-defined defaults and are left unchanged. WooCommerce grants Shop Manager Appearance access by default; that permission is retained. Other permission tools may independently grant access."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/help.php:15
msgid "Keep a database backup before downgrading. Legacy options are preserved exactly as they were at upgrade; changes made in version 4 are not written back into the older format."
msgstr ""

